    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Capstone: one component, one scale.\n\nIf source mixtures are given as ratios, first convert both to the fraction of the same component. Convert the target too. Then alligate and finally scale to total quantity if needed.\n\nMost difficult-looking mixture questions become routine once every source is expressed on one scale.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A useful check is to compute the final component amount directly.\n\nIf 12 L at 75% and 8 L at 45% are mixed, milk/active component = 9 + 3.6 = 12.6 L out of 20 L = 63%.\n\nThat direct check should match the weighted-average answer.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
